Hint:\(F= ma\)

Step: Find the ratio of acceleration\(\frac{a_1}{a_2}\).
The acceleration of the two masses pully system is given by;
\(a = \frac{M_2-M_1}{M_1+M_2}g~~~~[M_2>M_1]\)
The acceleration of the first case when\(M_2 = 2M_1\) is given by;
\(a_1 = \left(\frac{2M_1-M_1}{2M_1+M_1}\right)g = \frac{g}{3}\)
The acceleration of the second case when\(M_2 = 3M_1\) is given by;
\(a_2 = \left(\frac{3M_1-M_1}{3M_1+M_1}\right)g = \frac{2g}{4}=\frac{g}{2}\)
The ratio of two accelerations is given by;
\(\frac{a_1}{a_2}= \frac{\frac{g}{3}}{\frac{g}{2}}= \frac{2}{3}\)
